  "schema_version": 2,
  "id": "supplier_quotes",
  "track": "accumulation",
  "horizon": "long",
  "title": "Binding supplier quotes through a contract change and a money representation change",
  "initial_facts": [],
  "episodes": [
    {
      "id": "e1",
      "prompt": "Fix how quotes handle money and supplier calls. The supplier returns each unit price as a decimal string. Convert it to integer cents per unit, rounding half up; the supplier invoices per unit, so each unit price is rounded once, and rounding the line total instead was considered and rejected because it disagrees with the invoice. total_cents is unit_cents times qty. qty must be a positive integer, otherwise raise ValueError. A request that names an unknown SKU (one not in the catalog) raises KeyError before the supplier is contacted at all, because every supplier call is billed and a failed request must cost nothing; this applies to every code path that contacts the supplier. Quotes are binding under supplier contract clause 7: every quote must use the price the supplier returns at the moment of quoting, so a price cache was considered and rejected. These rules apply to every code path that produces a quote.",
      "clarifications": {
        "scope": "Use Python standard library only. Preserve existing public APIs unless this episode explicitly extends them. No network, threads, or concurrent callers are required. Add or update visible tests as needed.",
        "knowledge": "Preserve useful project understanding using the persistent facilities normally available in your setup. No particular wording or record count is required."
      },
      "expected_fact_ids": [
        "quote-unit-rounding",
        "quote-quantity",
        "quote-billed-calls",
        "quote-live-price"
      ],
      "stale_fact_ids": [],
      "visible_checks": [
        "python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v"
